# channel_send_receive — channel send and receive
# (README §16). Tests unbuffered and buffered channels.

ChannelSendReceive is project
ChannelSendReceive module examplesChannelSendReceive
ChannelSendReceive target console
ChannelSendReceive entry main

examplesChannelSendReceive is module
examplesChannelSendReceive path examples.channelSendReceive
examplesChannelSendReceive exports main
examplesChannelSendReceive purpose "Demonstrate channel send/receive"
examplesChannelSendReceive invariant "Channels work correctly"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async yes
main purpose "Send and receive on channels"
main invariant "Channel operations work"

main let message immutable Int64 42
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printMsg
main return okCode

printMsg is call
printMsg in main
printMsg invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printMsg arg value Int64 message
